  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and customers pay for reliable work, control logic, safety and documentation and clear communication. Pay varies by city, employer and years, so verify with current notices.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is doing the real task once and noting what you learned.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and industrial automation, PLC, SCADA and instrumentation: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools explain concepts, help practise tests and draft applications. Routine tasks shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Skill, honesty and proof hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to learn faster; later, own your results and your story.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Alternatives that can beat a general industrial automation, PLC, SCADA and instrumentation path</h2>

